config:
  themeCSS: "text.messageText { stroke: #ffffff; stroke-width: 4px; paint-order: stroke fill; } .rect { stroke: #b42318; stroke-width: 2px; }"
  sequence:
    width: 130
    actorMargin: 30
    noteMargin: 8
---
sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: One node's turn
  accDescr: One node's turn: pre-upgrade Jobs run on other nodes, the node is released into the canary, MCO drains, updates and reboots it, the operator waits until it is upgraded and ready, cleanup Jobs run, and the node returns to its paused pool.
  autonumber
  participant Op as Operator
  participant Pre as Pre-upgrade Jobs
  participant N as Node N
  participant MCO as MCO<br/>(canary pool)
  participant Post as Cleanup Jobs

  Note over Op,Post: UpgradeReady=True and MCPUpdated=True,<br/>the previous node has finished,<br/>its cleanup Jobs included
  Note over Op,Post: The operator reads the MutexRunConfig again<br/>and stops if it is being deleted
  Note over Op,Post: N already at X and not released:<br/>no Jobs, NodeUpgrade=True NodeAlreadyUpgraded
  Note over Op,Post: MCO already updating N: wait for it first.<br/>MCO updating another target node:<br/>stop and retry later.
  loop each rule, in spec.mutexRules order, whose mutex label N still carries
    Op->>Pre: create a Job, or<br/>re-use the one with<br/>the same job-key<br/>that has not failed
    Note over Op,Post: generateName #lt;jobName#gt;-,<br/>env NODE_NAME=N and MUTEX_RULE=#lt;rule#gt;,<br/>affinity kubernetes.io/hostname NotIn [N],<br/>label nodeupgrade.redhat-na-ssa.github.io/job-key
    Op->>Pre: poll every 10 s,<br/>up to timeoutSeconds
    alt Failed, or still running at timeoutSeconds
      rect rgb(253, 226, 225)
        Note over Op,Post: JobRun=False JobRunFailed, Degraded=True:<br/>the run stops, N stays held<br/>in its paused pool (fail-closed)
      end
    end
  end
  Note over Op,Post: [JobRun=True JobRunSucceeded]
  Note over N: schedulable, in its<br/>paused pool,<br/>workloads running
  Op->>N: one patch: remove the mutex<br/>labels and labelled-by,<br/>add release=v and<br/>released-by=#lt;ns#gt;/#lt;name#gt;|X
  MCO->>N: N now matches the<br/>canary: desiredConfig<br/>= rendered-canary-*
  MCO->>N: cordon, drain<br/>(PDBs apply), update,<br/>reboot, uncordon
  Note over N,MCO: NFD may change the version<br/>label before MCO is done:<br/>the label alone is not enough
  Op->>N: poll every 60 s, at most<br/>120 times (2 h), until all hold
  Note over Op,Post: release-image-version = X,<br/>machineconfiguration.openshift.io/state<br/>= Done, currentConfig = desiredConfig,<br/>a rendered-#lt;canary#gt;-* config, Ready=True
  alt not all hold after 2 h
    rect rgb(253, 226, 225)
      Note over Op,Post: NodeUpgrade=False NodeUpgradeFailed,<br/>Degraded=True: the run stops. N stays<br/>released, the retry resumes at this wait
    end
  end
  loop every rule that has a cleanUpJobSpec, in the same order
    Op->>Post: generateName cleanup-#lt;jobName#gt;-,<br/>same env, affinity and timeout
    alt Failed, or still running at timeoutSeconds
      rect rgb(253, 226, 225)
        Note over Op,Post: JobRun=False JobRunFailed, Degraded=True:<br/>the run stops. N stays released, the retry<br/>resumes at the wait, then the cleanup Jobs
      end
    end
  end
  Op->>N: one patch removes release<br/>and released-by: N returns<br/>to its paused pool, no reboot
  Note over Op,Post: [NodeUpgrade=True NodeUpgradeSucceeded<br/>"Node is i of n"]
  Note over Op,Post: Operator restart after the release patch:<br/>N resumes at the wait (released-by).<br/>MutexRunConfig deleted: its finalizer<br/>runs no cleanup Jobs.
